- core/stats/reml.py: REML for variance-component models by Fisher
  scoring (negative components allowed while V stays positive definite),
  GLS fixed effects, Wald statistics, Kenward–Roger denominator df (with
  the average-information matrix, as in GenStat; F = Wald/df), eBLUPs.
- core/stats/mixed.py: mixed_model — 1–3 crossed fixed factors and up to
  three nested structural factors: variance components with SE,
  covariance structure of observations, stratum variances for balanced
  nesting, fixed effects, incremental and marginal tests, marginal
  predictions with SE and SED, factor means and differences, residuals.
- Tests against Tables 16.1–16.3, 16.5, 16.6 and Examples 16.1F–I, 16.2
  (Table 16.4 data added); single random term checked vs statsmodels.
- Catalog (stratum_1–3 slots), i18n, bridge, messages.

